  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Rural Women through access to renewable energy via biodigesters</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In rural Tajikistan, a significant portion of households and farms maintain livestock, with each typically owning 1-2 cows, 3-4 sheep, and 5-10 hens. Consequently, nearly every household and dehkan farm has access to animal manure. Prevalent practice in Tajikistan involves drying the animal manure to prepare kizyak , a form of dung, for later use as a source of energy for cooking and heating homes.</narrative>
  </description>
